NAME
    err - an error message on the console (#include "../lib_err.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_err.c"
    eputs("cmd: not found");

DESCRIPTION
    eputs(s) prints s and a line feed on the RAW console, through the
    ROM's CHAROUT vector, whatever the shell did with stdout: a
    "not found" never lands in a > file or in the next command of a
    pipe, as with the P8X eputs (stderr, in effect; there is no 2>).
    eput2(s, t) prints s then eputs(t); eputc(c) is one raw byte.

    Convention: eputs for failures, including a usage message printed
    because the arguments were wrong; puts for output, including the
    usage asked for with -h.

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: bios(CHAROUT, 0, c) per byte instead
    of the PUTS and CONOUT BIOS calls. Until the shell had redirection
    (2026-09-23) it was putchar.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_err.c 2026-09-23.

